materials:
Use case: stylized-concept
Asset type: production source material texture atlas for REUSABLE 32x32 WORLD MAP TILES, not a scenery illustration.
Reference image 1 gives the USER-APPROVED STYLE B "朴素复古": soft, modest classic Super Famicom / GBA Fire Emblem-like tactical map pixels, muted olive foliage, ash gray/lilac stone, dusty plum roofs and slate gray-blue water. Preserve its understated palette and simple coarse pixel clusters. No sharp modern HD pixel illustration or miniature model realism.
Create a perfectly regular 4 COLUMN by 3 ROW atlas of exactly TWELVE square material swatches. Target square-cell overall canvas 1536x1152. EACH CELL fills its entire square with that ground material. NO gutters, labels, grid lines, frame, shadows or objects. Every cell must be like an enlarged seamless 32x32 pixel game texture: flat base color, very sparse restrained 1–3-pixel cluster accents, only 2–3 tones per material, clear broad pixels. The outermost 4 native pixels of each cell are PURE UNIFORM base color so square tiles can repeat without seam.
Exact reading-order arrangement:
Row1 Col1: sage OLIVE GRASS plain, quiet medium olive with a few small darker tuft clusters;
Row1 Col2: SLATE BLUE SEA, mostly uniform desaturated gray blue with just two tiny short pale horizontal ripple dashes, no shore;
Row1 Col3: DUSTY SAND, subdued beige ochre with a couple slightly darker sand clusters, no dunes;
Row1 Col4: PEARL GRAY SNOW, almost white with sparse muted lavender-blue soft square shaded patches, no trees;
Row2 Col1: SALT FLAT, light bone gray with very sparse pale tan mineral specks, clearly different from snow;
Row2 Col2: TIDAL MARSH GROUND, dark muted olive-gray with a few flat gray-blue wet patches, no reeds or shrubs;
Row2 Col3: FOREST FLOOR, deeper pine olive moss plain with a few muted leaf specks, no trees;
Row2 Col4: ASH ROCK GROUND, muted gray-lilac with very sparse coarse strata marks, no mountains;
Row3 Col1: OLD STONE PAVING, soft ash gray square slabs and faint quiet taupe joint marks, no brick wall, no perspective;
Row3 Col2: TAUPE DIRT ROAD MATERIAL, quiet warm taupe brown with a couple coarse dusty pebble marks, not a shaped road;
Row3 Col3: OLD TIMBER PLANK MATERIAL, soft weathered brown with a few thin broad vertical wood-grain streaks, no nails;
Row3 Col4: PALE SACRED STONE, light gray-lilac old stone with restrained dull brass fleck, no glow or magical effects.
These are world-map material tiles, under trees/mountains/buildings and for automatic edge and corner composition. Use subdued coherent game palette. No smooth gradients, painterly texture, anti-aliased edges, noise, caustics, realistic gravel, fancy ornament, buildings, characters or lettering. Keep all 12 swatches perfectly square in a 4x3 arrangement, visually distinct and sparse.

terrain_modules:
Use case: stylized-concept
Asset type: production transparent terrain-decoration module atlas for reusable WORLD MAP TILES.
Reference image 1 is the selected B "朴素复古" art direction: classic Super Famicom / GBA Fire Emblem-style 2D orthogonal-map pixels, quiet olive/pine, ash gray-lilac rocks, gray-blue water, very sparse details. Match it closely. NO modern sharp or realistic high-detail pixel rendering.
Create exactly TWELVE fully separate complete terrain sprites in a perfectly aligned 4-column x 3-row atlas, 1536x1152 if possible. Each equal cell contains exactly ONE sprite and has a wide clean transparent margin around the whole object. Transparent background, no labels, grid, checkerboard or colored fringe.
These are tiny low-resolution WORLD-MAP ornaments, each conceived at either 32x32 or 64x64 native pixels and then enlarged. Large calm pixel clusters, 2–3 main tones per material, colored subdued outlines, simple soft shapes. Native sprite silhouette complete and legible. Keep the objects within 70 percent of each cell so none touch a neighbor. Camera classical straight overhead map view, roofs/trees shown from north, NOT isometric.
Exact reading order:
Row1 col1: one compact broadleaf olive tree with round three-tone canopy and short trunk, no ground patch;
Row1 col2: one compact muted pine tree with three broad soft tiers and a tiny trunk, no ground patch;
Row1 col3: small contiguous grove of 4 compact rounded broadleaf trees, a complete 2x2-tile forest module, no ground patch;
Row1 col4: small contiguous grove of 4 muted pine trees, a complete 2x2-tile forest module, no ground patch.
Row2 col1: one simple pine with pearl snow on broad tiers, no snow ground patch;
Row2 col2: small complete grove of 4 snow-capped pines, 2x2-tile module, no snow ground patch;
Row2 col3: low small cluster of 3 ash gray-lilac rocks, complete unobtrusive sprite;
Row2 col4: connected low ridge of 3 softly rounded gray-lilac mountain peaks, broad connected base, complete 2x2-tile module; not realistic craggy cliff.
Row3 col1: connected low ridge of 3 rounded gray mountain peaks capped with modest pearl snow, complete 2x2-tile module;
Row3 col2: compact group of muted olive marsh reeds, simple broad blades with a few tan tops, no water rectangle;
Row3 col3: long low horizontal stone ledge, moss green top rim, quiet ash gray vertical rock face, complete 2x1-tile module;
Row3 col4: three small muted green water-lily leaves for a quiet tidal lagoon, no water rectangle.
All sprites have coherent upper-left gentle lighting and low detail density. No bright gleam, gradients, realistic leaves, microtexture, blur, characters or buildings. True transparent alpha around all silhouettes; no white/blue/red chromakey residues. Full modules will be cut on native square tile boundaries in production, so avoid tall canopy tips far outside their own footprint.

landmarks:
Use case: stylized-concept
Asset type: production transparent WORLD MAP LANDMARK MODULE atlas, for reusable 32x32 tiles.
Reference image 1 is the USER-APPROVED B "朴素复古": quiet classic Super Famicom / GBA Fire Emblem map art, muted dusty PLUM roofs, soft ASH GRAY/LILAC stone, OLIVE foliage, SLATE GRAY BLUE water and dull BRASS sun relics. Match those simple flat pixel clusters. Very economical old-console sprite craft, NOT realistic architecture or a modern high-definition miniature illustration.
Make ONE perfectly aligned 4-column x 4-row atlas of exactly 16 complete isolated landmark modules on genuine TRANSPARENT background. Target 1536x1536. Each equal cell contains only one whole object with at least 15 percent transparent margin on all sides; no neighboring cells touch. No labels, numbers, frame, drawn grid or checkerboard.
Tiny native world-map sprites: small camps/boats conceived at 32x32 native pixels; village/temple/city conceived at 64x64, tower/lighthouse at 32x64, fort/prison/galleon at 64x32. Enlarge coarse pixels visibly. 2–3 broad colors per material, understated colored outlines, low architectural detail. Classic overhead orthogonal RPG map view, short front facades, no isometric projection. Entire objects and optional small natural foundation fit inside the cell. No rectangular grass, sea, snow or other ground backdrops, no glow, no black shadow puddle.
Exact reading order:
Row1 Col1: small ordinary village of three compact timber cottages with plain muted dusty plum roofs;
Row1 Col2: small snow village of three similar plum-roof cottages with restrained pearl snow caps;
Row1 Col3: compact coastal harbor town, modest stone wall, two plum roof homes and small wooden pier, no sea backdrop;
Row1 Col4: low stone military fort gate with two square plain towers, muted plum flags.
Row2 Col1: royal capital symbol, a modest larger square stone citadel with 3 towers and plum roofs, little original sun banner, no ornate fantasy spires;
Row2 Col2: original ancient sun sanctuary, short plain stone arch and low ritual steps with a tiny dull brass sun mark, no cross;
Row2 Col3: slender octagonal plain sunlight relay tower, gray stone, small dull brass mirror at top, NO glowing gold sphere;
Row2 Col4: low rocky old mine mouth with a simple timber doorway, no detailed tracks.
Row3 Col1: modest stone lighthouse with tiny warm brass lamp, gray rock base, no sea backdrop;
Row3 Col2: squat salt-flat observatory, simple short ash gray platform, tiny brass ring instrument, no giant lens or domed palace;
Row3 Col3: small desert settlement of three simple beige stone buildings with flat dusty plum awnings, no palm-tree jungle;
Row3 Col4: low stone detention stockade, plain barred central gate and two small square guard towers.
Row4 Col1: small military supply camp, two muted taupe canvas tents, 3 simple crates and tiny plum pennant;
Row4 Col2: modest one-mast wooden cutter with plain off-white triangular sail, no sea backdrop;
Row4 Col3: compact dark prison galleon with one broad plum square sail and low deck, no sea backdrop;
Row4 Col4: small ancient sun-library symbol, plain rectangular stone building, short columns, simple plum roof and dull brass sun plaque, no cloud or ground rectangle.
This game has Western continent, Eastern islands, a large geographical fracture, memories of lost family and a controlling sun god; use restrained original fantasy motifs. No characters, religious crosses, contemporary technology, Japanese torii, ornate medieval cathedral facades, sparkling gems or magical effects. Entire native silhouettes clear, no cropping, no white/red/blue/green fringes.
